Cell["5. Drawing arrays", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2b44162b-4fe0-184a-884c-b451e8787946"],

Cell["\<\
There are two families of pictures, and an array of any order may be drawn in \
either. The flat family gives plane graphics throughout; the spatial family \
gives cubes arranged in space. Which to use is a matter of what you want to \
see, not of what the array is.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b63a9e24-b4e9-d84c-929e-e86759dbab6f"],

Cell["The flat family: ArrayGraphics", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"1950923c-da1c-e345-82b7-5a0d9e6ff60f"],

Cell["At order one a row of cells, at order two a grid:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dd21d06e-77e1-4649-9e06-87332f2c5730"],

Cell["\<\
{ArrayGraphics[{1, 2, 3, 4}], ArrayGraphics[{{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}}]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"6f8a04c1-d2e6-5c40-9dec-34c09fce5881"],

