Cell["Above order three: tiling rather than nesting", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"424aacd3-dcf8-3344-868c-251ae6c880e3"],

Cell["\<\
Space runs out at three indices just as the plane runs out at two. But where \
the flat family insets a picture into each cell, the spatial family has \
nowhere to inset anything: a Graphics3D cannot hold another Graphics3D. So \
the blocks are tiled instead. A 4-array is a line of lattices, shifted along \
by the extent of one and a gap:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b5278c64-5e23-c84a-b88f-7164a8ff2033"],

Cell["ArrayGraphics3D[Array[#1 + #2 + #3 + #4 &, {2, 2, 2, 2}]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"75661cdf-7d19-e844-9f8b-2408cd0f6f2f"],

